# Auto Yield's own proof. Seat 1 (ai, "bob" in the test's own names) has an
# uncontested Main Phase 1 and TWO Lightning Bolts castable, one per
# untapped Mountain: no creature on either battlefield, so the only legal
# targets are the two players (`bolt-player.state`'s own claim). The second
# Bolt/Mountain pair is what proves the override expires on its own turn
# (`UNTAP` re-readies bob's second Mountain for his turn-3 main) rather than
# needing a second press. Seat 0 (human, "alice") holds Counterspell and two
# untapped Islands — enough to counter a Bolt with no "unless you pay" clause
# in the way, the same shape `w46-b-counterspell.state` already uses for
# Memnite. The point of the scenario is alice's own response window on bob's
# turn: with auto-yield on, that window is never shown to her at all; without
# it, on a LATER bob turn, it is.
turn=1
activeplayer=ai
activephase=MAIN1
humanlife=20
ailife=20
humanhand=Counterspell
humanbattlefield=Island;Island
humanlibrary=Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain
humangraveyard=
aihand=Lightning Bolt;Lightning Bolt
aibattlefield=Mountain;Mountain
ailibrary=Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain
aigraveyard=
